Adaptive learning rules:

- If a learner scores below 60% in a topic, recommend reviewing the topic and completing additional practice.
- If the learner scores between 60% and 79%, recommend targeted revision and another assessment.
- If the learner scores 80% or above, consider recommending the next topic or a more advanced activity.
- If repeated attempts show poor performance, flag the topic for mentor review.
- If a learner completes a course without demonstrating sufficient knowledge, recommend an assessment instead of marking the skill as mastered.
- If a required skill has no assessment evidence, recommend an appropriate diagnostic assessment.

